1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,174
Akka is one platform for agentic AI.

2
00:00:03,174 --> 00:00:10,838
Specify builds it, the Agent SDK runs it, Verify governs it, and Optimize runs it on the right models.

3
00:00:10,838 --> 00:00:14,468
Today, let's look at one part of Optimize: Experiments.

4
00:00:16,018 --> 00:00:18,140
Every model change is a bet.

5
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:22,384
A cheaper model could cut your bill, or quietly hurt your customers.

6
00:00:22,384 --> 00:00:25,213
So most teams never switch, or switch blind.

7
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:30,026
Experiments turns that bet into a measured rollout.

8
00:00:30,026 --> 00:00:38,847
Choose a technique: a smaller model, a self-hosted open-weight model, an added decisioning model, planner and worker routing, or a trial balloon.

9
00:00:38,847 --> 00:00:43,258
Then set your limits, and what happens if one is crossed.

10
00:00:44,808 --> 00:00:47,706
It starts in shadow, with nothing at risk.

11
00:00:47,706 --> 00:00:53,864
Then a canary takes a growing share of live traffic, graded against your limits, region by region.

12
00:00:55,608 --> 00:00:59,204
We can see that quality in Germany is starting to degrade.

13
00:00:59,204 --> 00:01:04,107
The rest of the experiment continues, with Germany's traffic routing back to the original model.

14
00:01:06,408 --> 00:01:11,188
A person decides. Promote it to all traffic, and Watch keeps guarding it.

15
00:01:11,188 --> 00:01:15,232
Every stage, every verdict and every dollar is on one record.

16
00:01:17,208 --> 00:01:21,480
Cheaper models, earned in production. Akka Optimize Experiments.
